        <activityName xml:lang="en">Ethylene oxide, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Ethylene oxide, at plant
The processes that are used to produce ethylene oxide from ethylene, oxygen or air are described in this inventory. These processes also produce carbon dioxide in some quantity.;
CAS number: 000075-21-8; 
Formula: C2H4O; 
UUID: 6ab29660-cc4e-30a3-aaa1-f175fa54dd61
Precursors, transports, infrastructure.
Location: RER
Technology: represents a current cross-section of actual plants in Europe
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: see technology 
Extrapolations: see technology
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_6ab29660-cc4e-30a3-aaa1-f175fa54dd61.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
